WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.000
Interest in President Kennedy's proposed Peace Corps continues to rise among American youth.

00:10.000 --> 00:12.000
Here are the forerunners of the Peace Corps.

00:12.000 --> 00:17.000
American exchange students now overseas in backward and depressed areas of the world,

00:17.000 --> 00:25.000
giving of their strength, skills and education in tasks similar to the missions that will be assigned to Peace Corps members.

00:25.000 --> 00:40.000
The popular response to the Peace Corps proposal with thousands of inquiries pouring in before application forms were even ready

00:40.000 --> 00:46.000
is a measure of the younger generation's readiness to accept a bold challenge to positive action.

00:46.000 --> 00:53.000
Now, following up his initial announcement, President Kennedy appears before newsreel cameras in the White House

00:53.000 --> 00:59.000
to outline the program and the prospects of the global Peace Corps.

00:59.000 --> 01:04.000
The Peace Corps is really the idea of the American people.

01:04.000 --> 01:14.000
When I talked last fall about the idea of young American men and women going abroad to serve shoulder to shoulder

01:14.000 --> 01:22.000
with the citizens of newly emerging countries, a tremendous response went up from the schools and colleges of the United States.

01:22.000 --> 01:27.000
In the last few months, more applications for the Peace Corps have come to us

01:27.000 --> 01:32.000
than have come for positions in all the rest of the United States government put together.

01:32.000 --> 01:37.000
What is remarkable is that there is no salary for the members of the Peace Corps.

01:37.000 --> 01:41.000
They will go abroad and live on the same standard as people of other countries,

01:41.000 --> 01:48.000
but they will work with them two or three years, devoting part of their lives to peace

01:48.000 --> 01:56.000
and to strengthening the ties that bind men together all over the globe who are capable and well trained

01:56.000 --> 02:00.000
and who will be welcomed by other countries.

02:00.000 --> 02:07.000
Our Peace Corps, I want to emphasize, is not designed as a weapon of propaganda,

02:07.000 --> 02:11.000
is not designed as a tool in the Cold War.

02:11.000 --> 02:20.000
It is a genuine effort by the people of the United States, particularly those who are young,

02:20.000 --> 02:27.000
to play their part in working for peace and improving the lives of all mankind.

02:27.000 --> 02:34.000
It comes, I think, from a deep historic and revolutionary experience that we have had.

02:34.000 --> 02:38.000
The people of this country are anxious to see a world in peace.

02:38.000 --> 02:45.000
Young people in this country are anxious to hold out their hands to people in other worlds.

02:45.000 --> 03:10.000
They will learn as much as they will teach.

